  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/cb4b80b2-4963-4b8f-88f7-7b03d603ed84.png\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 156px;\" /></p><p><math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;(Let <math><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math>)<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>0</mn></math> or <math><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn></math> or <math><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></math><br />If <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and so on<br />Since, the curve is symmetric in the&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></msup></math> quadrant</p><p>Hence, the required area <math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p>",
